
[FIXED] The volatile partition and rendered climate use separate temperatures. The inventory calculation (src/classes/shore.cpp:480) uses an irradiation-based temperature proxy; the surface calculation (src/classes/planet.cpp:1703) uses empirical gray-atmosphere opacity. The app already records disagreements between them. They do not constitute a converged atmosphere–climate solution; we should implement one.

The temperature estimator does not resolve runaway greenhouse. It calculates warming from prescribed gas abundances. A finite, comfortable answer therefore does not establish that evaporation and atmospheric feedback would preserve that state. We should add checks to determine whether it would.

Seasonal freezing is approximate. The seasonal model (src/classes/planet.cpp:1031) includes thermal lag and an approximate freezing buffer, but does not evolve a fully coupled ice thickness, melt-energy budget, and ice-albedo feedback. Crossing 273 K is insufficient to establish an actual seasonal pond or ocean opening. Find out what would make this part complete and add it.

